.TH "bash\-server\-cmd\-json" "5" "2026\-02\-01" "bash\-server 0.1.0" "bash\-server file formats"
.SH DESCRIPTION
This page documents the JSON serialization format used by
\f[B]bash\-server\f[R](1) to represent Bash\(cqs internal
\f[B]COMMAND\f[R] abstract syntax tree (AST).
The format is implemented in \f[B]cmd_serialize.c\f[R] and supports
bidirectional conversion:
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]cmd_serialize(COMMAND*)\f[R] \(em serialize a COMMAND tree to JSON.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]cmd_deserialize(JSON)\f[R] \(em deserialize JSON back to a COMMAND
tree.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]cmd_free(COMMAND*)\f[R] \(em free a deserialized COMMAND tree.
.PP
This format appears in the \f[B]\(lqast\(rq\f[R] field of debug channel
messages (see \f[B]bash\-server\-json\-messages\f[R](5), CHAN_DEBUG) and
in the \f[B]\(lqexecute\(rq\f[R] command on CHAN_COMMAND.
.SH FORMAT
.SH Top\-level structure
Every COMMAND node serializes to a JSON object with these common fields:
.IP
.EX
{
