.SH Null values
Missing or absent commands, redirect lists, and optional fields are
represented as JSON \f[B]null\f[R].
For example, a cm_if with no else branch has
\f[CR]\(dqfalse_case\(dq: null\f[R].
.SH EXAMPLES
.SH Simple command: \f[CR]echo hello\f[R]
.IP
.EX
{
  \(dqtype\(dq: \(dqcm_simple\(dq,
  \(dqflags\(dq: 0,
  \(dqline\(dq: 1,
  \(dqredirects\(dq: \f[B]null\f[R],
  \(dqsimple\(dq: {
    \(dqflags\(dq: 0,
    \(dqline\(dq: 1,
    \(dqwords\(dq: [
      {\(dqword\(dq: \(dqecho\(dq, \(dqflags\(dq: 0},
      {\(dqword\(dq: \(dqhello\(dq, \(dqflags\(dq: 0}
    ],
    \(dqredirects\(dq: \f[B]null\f[R]
  }
}
